  "details": "a long time ago someone requested, that we should be able to upload several CustomOverrides for one avatar. I voted on that, but... now that I get back into making animations I got a better idea.\n\nMy idea is to let us upload the animations seperately and then combine them into animationsets / -profiles\n\nThat means, that we would have a menu, where we would see the controller we are using and a list (folder structure) with all animations uploaded by us.\n\nThe animations would then be dragged onto the controller to bind it to that button.\n\nAlso if a custom override is uploaded with the model vrchat automatically creates a folder for that avatar containing the animations and the override.\n\nwhen clicking on \"load animationset\" all custom overrides will be displayed in the main area.\n\nwhen hitting \"edit animationset\" all seperate animations will be displayed in the main area.\n\n\nEDIT: this menu could also be only a animationset selector and all the configuration happens in the SDK.",
